# SENTRY Chat UI Redesign Plan

This plan details the steps to address the design feedback regarding the Chat module. The goal is to move from a heavily terminal-based log interface to a user-friendly conversational layout (similar to WhatsApp or Slack), while integrating "slash commands" that open contextual floating panels rather than triggering full page navigations.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Chat Interface Overhaul (WhatsApp/Modern Style)

- [MODIFY] [ChatWindow.tsx](file:///d:/github/SENTRY-jules-polish-frontend-pitch-5288243582464063829/SENTRY-jules-polish-frontend-pitch-5288243582464063829/packages/web/src/features/chat/ui/ChatWindow.tsx)
  - Layout Structure: Convert the `logs` rendering into a standard messaging structure.
    - Incoming messages align left with a distinct background (e.g., `terminal-800`).
    - Outgoing ("self") messages align right with the primary accent color (e.g., `success-muted` or `primary`).
    - Remove the "boot sequence" typing effect in the chat to immediately show history.
  - Input Area: Implement a standard fixed sticky-bottom input box, removing the `msg>` prefix and blinking `div` cursor. Use a polished text area.

### 2. Contextual Command Panels (Floating Overlays)

- [NEW] Component: `SlidingPanel` (or `FloatingWidget`).
  - Create a reusable, draggable, or sliding overlay container that renders over the right side or center of the chat interface.
- [MODIFY] [ChatWindow.tsx](file:///d:/github/SENTRY-jules-polish-frontend-pitch-5288243582464063829/SENTRY-jules-polish-frontend-pitch-5288243582464063829/packages/web/src/features/chat/ui/ChatWindow.tsx)
  - Command Handling: intercept `/workshops`, `/feed`, `/projects` in the chat input.
  - State Management: When a command is triggered, instead of calling `useNavigate()` to route away from the chat, load the respective Component (e.g., `<WorkshopPage />`, `<ActivityFeed />`) into the `FloatingWidget` overlay state.
  - The chat remains visible in the background or side.

### 3. Cleaning Up Terminal Logic

- [MODIFY] [ChatWindow.tsx](file:///d:/github/SENTRY-jules-polish-frontend-pitch-5288243582464063829/SENTRY-jules-polish-frontend-pitch-5288243582464063829/packages/web/src/features/chat/ui/ChatWindow.tsx)
  - Remove all pseudo-terminal styling mechanisms ([getLogColor](file:///d:/github/SENTRY-jules-polish-frontend-pitch-5288243582464063829/SENTRY-jules-polish-frontend-pitch-5288243582464063829/packages/web/src/features/documents/DocumentsPage.tsx#327-343), specific divider lines `══════════`).
  - Render an [EmptyState](file:///d:/github/SENTRY-jules-polish-frontend-pitch-5288243582464063829/SENTRY-jules-polish-frontend-pitch-5288243582464063829/packages/web/src/shared/ui/EmptyState.tsx#15-54) when the channel has zero messages instead of falling back to terminal logs.

## Verification Plan

- **UI Verification:** Send messages as the current user and ensure they render on the right with a distinctive bubble. Ensure the history renders left-aligned for other users.
- **Command Verification:** Type `/workshops` and hit Enter. Verify that a sliding panel or overlay appears showing the Workshops feature, without unmounting the active WebSocket chat link.
